	<hiddenLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">¤</hiddenLabel>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_P">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_P</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">P</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">P Printing products</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Considerations on printing products.
The products surveyed here are the products resulting from printing only, which means that only the work of the printer is to be taken into account (provision of raw materials [paper, ink, etc], provision of manpower, printing services, etc). In CPA 2.1 publishing is classified out of manufacturing and therefore out of PRODCOM scope. No CN reference is made for printing products because the corresponding CN codes are associated to products from publishing (which also cover other costs like remuneration of intellectual property, advertisement, etc). 
Note that the headings for printing products refer to physical products and not to industrial services, and therefore require the volume of production to be reported.</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_24.S1">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_24.S1</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">S1</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">S1 Supply of castings</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Considerations on sub-contracting. 
These headings are for recording metal products and metal processing products to be fitted into certain appliances and machines or to be processed. However, only those products should be reported that are sold by the producer enterprise to other enterprises. Components that are processed in the producer enterprise or are fitted into the enterprise's own products should not be reported. </plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_2x.S1">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_2x.S1</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">S1</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">S1 Supply of parts and accessories</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Considerations on sub-contracting.
These headings are for recording metal products and metal processing products to be fitted into certain appliances and machines or to be processed. However, only those products should be reported which are sold by the producer enterprise to another (supplier) enterprise. Components processed by the producer enterprise or fitted into its own products should not be reported.</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_C">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_C</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">C</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">C Treatment and coating of metals</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Considerations on metal coating.
These headings are for recording surface treatment and hardening; this only applies, however, to the treatment of bought-in products (treatment on own account) and the treatment of outside products under contract (contract treatment). For further details, see point 9.1 of the general notes to the PRODCOM list.
</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_22.S1">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_22.S1</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">S1</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">S1 Supply of plastic components</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Considerations on sub-contracting
These headings are for recording plastic components to be fitted into certain appliances and machines or to be processed. Only those products should be reported which are sold by the producer enterprise to other enterprises. Components which are processed in the producer enterprise or are fitted into its own products should not be reported.</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_24.T_B1">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_24.T_B1</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">B1</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">B1 Non-alloy steel</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Specific definitions for some iron and steel products.
Steel grades in which none of the following limit values is reached by any specified element as defined in clause 4.1 and Table 1 and its footnotes of EN 10020:
-	1,65	%	of manganese,
-	0,50	% 	of silicon,
-	0,40	% 	of copper or lead,
-	0,30	% 	of chromium or nickel,
-	0,10	%	of aluminium, bismuth, cobalt, tellurium, vanadium or tungsten,
-	0,08 	% 	of molybdenum,
-	0,06	% 	of niobium,
-	0,0008 % of boron,
-	0,05	% 	of any other alloy element except carbon, nitrogen, phosphorus or sulphur.
It follows that alloy steel is any grade with a specified chemical composition reaching any of the above limit values.</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_24.T_B3">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_24.T_B3</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">B3</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">B3 Stainless steel</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Specific definitions for some iron and steel products .
Alloy steel grades containing by weight 10,50 % or more of chromium but not more than 1,20 % of carbon, with or without other alloying elements. (EN 10 020: 5.2.2.2.1)</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_24.T_B2">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_24.T_B2</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">B2</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">B2 Other alloy steel</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Specific definitions for some iron and steel products .
Any steel grade defined as alloy (EN 10020: 4.2.2) not meeting the definitions of stainless steel given below (in B3).</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_C2">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_C2</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">C2</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">C2 Hot rolled narrow strip</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Specific definitions for some iron and steel products.
Flat products hot rolled in widths up to 600 mm, which, immediately after the final rolling pass are wound into coils. 
Production is measured immediately on completion of the rolling cycle, i.e. before trimming or rectification.</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_24.T_C3">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_24.T_C3</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">C3</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">C3 Plate and sheet rolled in lengths in wide strip mills</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Specific definitions for some iron and steel products.
These are hot rolled flat products generally less then 50 mm thick, the edges being allowed to deform freely, supplied flat in square or rectangular shapes with a width of 600 mm or more, and have been manufactured in the roughing stands of wide strip mills but not coiled. 
Included is plate recovered by cutting damaged hot rolled flat products where the defective areas are scrapped for immediate remelting.</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_24.T_A1">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_24.T_A1</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">A1</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A1 Pig iron</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Specific definitions for some iron and steel products .
Detailed definitions of the various grades of pig iron are set out in Table 2 and its footnotes of European Standard EN 10001, Definition and Classification of Pig Iron.
The following notes summarize the main categories:
(a)	pig iron
Iron-carbon alloy containing by weight more than 2 % of carbon and, either separately or together, not more than:
-	30	% 	of manganese
-	10	% 	of chromium,
-	8	% 	of silicon,
-	3	% 	of phosphorus,
-	10	% 	in total of other specified alloy elements (nickel, copper, aluminium, titanium, vanadium, molybdenum, etc.).
Materials exceeding these limits are ferro-alloys.
(b)	non-alloy pig iron
Pig iron with no specified alloy contents by weight more than:
-	6	% of manganese,
-	4	% of silicon,
-	0,3	% of chromium or nickel,
-	0,2	% of titanium,
-	0,1	% of other alloy elements.
Residual quantities up to 0,5 % of unspecified alloy elements found on analysis do not alter the classification of non-alloy pig iron.
(c)	steelmaking iron
Non-alloy pig iron containing by weight not more than 1,0 % of silicon.
A distinction is made between:
-	high phosphorus steelmaking iron containing 1,5 % up to and including 2,5 % of phosphorus,
-	low phosphorus steelmaking iron containing not more than 0,25 % of phosphorus.
(d)	foundry iron
Non-alloy pig iron containing by weight more than 1,0 % up to and including 4,0 % of silicon and not more than 1,5 % of manganese.
There are three main classes of foundry iron:
-	high phosphorus foundry iron containing more than 0,5 % of phosphorus,
-	low phosphorus foundry iron containing not more than 0,25 % of phosphorus,
-	low phosphorus foundry iron for spheroidal graphite castings containing not more than 0,1 % of manganese and not more than 3,0 % of silicon.
(e)	alloy pig iron
Pig iron with specified alloy contents exceeding any of the limits in (b) above.
(f)	spiegel iron
Alloy pig iron containing by weight more than 6,0 % up to and including 30,0 % of manganese with no other specified alloy elements exceeding the limits in (b) above.</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/qw1/prodcom2026/note_C1">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#ExplanatoryNote"/>
	<identifier xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">note_C1</identifier>
	<notation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#">C1</notation>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">C1 Hot rolled wide strip</prefLabel>
	<modified xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-08</modified>
	<created xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2025-01-07</created>
	<language xmlns="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ENG"/>
	<plainText xmlns="http://rdf-vocabulary.ddialliance.org/xkos#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Specific definitions for some iron and steel products.
Production from continuous mills, semi-continuous mills and reversing mills (Steckel, etc.) producing hot rolled flat products of width 600 mm or more, which immediately after the final rolling pass are wound into coils. 
The edges of the strip are slightly convex, as rolled, and production is measured immediately on completion of the rolling cycle, i.e. before trimming or rectification.</plainText>
</rdf:Description>

